WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.540
I’ve been using Apple’s AirPods for over
two years and I love them, and now Apple has

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.259
released the updated AirPods with the new
H1 chip, which actually DOES make AirPods

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.139
work better and more reliably.

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:15.030
That same chip is packed into the Powerbeats
Pro, which is awesome!

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:19.920
On top of that, the Powerbeats actually get
physical controls, including a more reliable

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:24.820
physical button to pause, switch tracks and
use Siri if you don’t want to use the new

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:25.949
Hey Siri feature.

00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:31.000
It also gets something that I really, truly
wish the AirPods had, volume controls on the

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.489
earphones themselves, and it’s in a pretty
convenient location as well.

00:00:35.489 --> 00:00:39.530
Unlike the AirPods, the Powerbeats wrap around
your ear so they don’t budge at all no matter

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:44.440
what kind of activity you’re doing, but
in most cases, the AirPods won’t fall out

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.440
either.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:46.440
The wrap around design is mostly to keep in
flow with their previous earphones.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.239
One thing I did notice was that the Powerbeats
Pro were nowhere near as comfortable in your

00:00:49.239 --> 00:00:52.460
ears as the AirPods over long periods of time.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.059
Your ears actually start to get a bit tired
over time and that doesn’t happen with the

00:00:56.059 --> 00:00:57.059
AirPods.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:00.460
It’s also much quicker and easier to get
the AirPods in your ears.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:04.570
The Powerbeats Pro definitely require a bit
more work get wrapped around your ears and

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.220
may take some time to get used to.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.000
Now the sound quality is noticeably better
on the Powerbeats Pro.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.110
Unlike AirPods, they create a seal inside
of your ear so they sound louder, block out

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.920
background noise and there’s much more bass.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.159
Like MUCH more.

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:23.470
Seriously, if you really love bass, just pay
the extra cash for the Powerbeats Pro.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:28.470
Now are they the best sounding wireless earphones
you can buy at the $250 price point?

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:33.740
No, definitely not, you can probably find
better-sounding ones for a lower price, but

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.510
it doesn’t matter because there’s something
missing with the other guys, that beautiful

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.510
Beats logo.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.100
Over the years, Beats by Dre has made a name
for itself by creating beautifully designed,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:47.710
high-quality headphones with great audio quality,
and almost everyone knows that.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:51.960
Yes, you can go on Amazon and research for
hours trying to find better-sounding earphones

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:55.970
for a cheaper price, but with Beats, you can
trust that they’re gonna work great and

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:58.540
sound great, and that’s why you’ll pay
extra for them.

00:01:58.540 --> 00:02:02.520
Not only that, but people around you know
that Beats are expensive, and if you’re

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.200
wearing them, it means you’re doing well
financially, and that’s why Beats will have

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.789
no problem selling these.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:11.500
However, you also get that same effect with
the AirPods, so what’s ultimately going

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.911
to happen is that Apple fans will buy the
AirPods and Beats fans will buy the PowerBeats

00:02:15.911 --> 00:02:16.911
Pro.

00:02:16.911 --> 00:02:17.911
Now, what if you like both?

00:02:17.911 --> 00:02:20.480
Well, let’s look at the downsides of the
PowerBeats.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.330
The biggest downside is the massive case,
just look at how much larger it is than the

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:29.070
AirPods case, and even at that size, it still
doesn’t include wireless charging.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.070
Why?

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:33.110
Well I think it’s because they’d have
to charge $300 for it, and that can make even

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:34.690
Beats fans think twice.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:39.220
The tiny AirPods case is incredibly convenient
because you can easily fit it in your pocket

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.710
and take it anywhere, but with the PowerBeats
Pro, the case is so huge that it’s really

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.790
impractical to squeeze into your pocket and
carry around.

00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:50.760
But on the plus side, the battery life on
the Powerbeats Pro lasts 9 hours compared

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.090
to 5 with AirPods, so you don’t have to
pop them back into the case for charging quite

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.370
as often, so you can leave the case behind.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:01.620
And when you do have to charge them, a quick
5-minute charge gets you one and a half hours

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.620
of playback.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.600
Another minor drawback is that you can only
charge the case using a Lightning cable, which

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.030
isn’t as widely available as USB-C, but
the case itself holds 15 hours of extra juice,

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:10.030
just like the AirPods.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.960
I also noticed another small issue with the
Powerbeats.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:16.310
With the AirPods, you can easily flick open
the top with one hand while you put your AirPods

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.430
back with the other.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:23.450
With PowerBeats Pro, you’ll have to use
both hands to get it open.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.810
That may sound a little farfetched but these
are the little differences you’ll notice

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:27.810
daily.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.650
With that said, the Powerbeats Pro are still
excellent earbuds that are a little on the

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.480
pricey side thanks to that Beats by Dre badge.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:38.150
If you like long battery life, physical controls,
and great-sounding bass, you’ll love these

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.150
earphones.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:42.512
Now if you prefer comfort and convenience
and saving some cash, I think you’ll be

00:03:42.512 --> 00:03:44.480
very happy with the AirPods.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.480
If you enjoyed this review, tap that like
button and click that circle above to subscribe.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:53.510
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video.

